WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
One-fifth of pre-war oil traffic, hinges on Tehran's Tuesday ask to reopen Hormuz. This is Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East, Episode 7. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Abbas Aragji, Iran's foreign minister, told state media he is waiting on a formal answer from Washington, France, 24 reports. Katari Gobetrins have already put ideas to Tehran. They are taking those ideas back to the American side, and then they are meant to bring Washington's

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.040
final word to Iran.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.980
Aragchi is in New York for the General Assembly.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.740
He said the Qataris hoped the reply would arrive by Tuesday, and that the talks right

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.260
now are about the straight alone.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.660
Re-opening, he said, depends on conditions Tehran has already sent.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.000
The war opened with American and Israeli strikes on Iran in late February.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.940
Tehran then shut Hormuz, Washington shut Iranian ports.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:59.120
It also once frozen assets released, oil sanctions lifted, and the American naval blockade ended.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:05.000
Last week in New York, Aragchi sat down with American envoy Steve Whitcough and Jared Kushner.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.800
Across the region, a court in Kenya has frozen the ground for a refinery the builders wanted to break tomorrow.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:20.200
Justice Jane O'Neilgo, at the Melindi Environment and Land Court, has stopped work toward the Dengote refinery in Lamu County, all Africa reports.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.920
She certified a petition by Salim Tima Swale and 132 others as urgent.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:35.620
Status quo holds on plot LR number 130,661 in Hindi slash Manda Magagoni until the 14th of October.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:44.100
Respondents may not clear, dig, fence, demolish, build, transfer, sell, or otherwise touch the pieces the petitioners occupy.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:50.400
Those 133 people say they have lived and farmed there for years, with homes, crops and trees,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.980
and that occupation itself is an interest any compulsory purchase has to count.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.920
They asked the court to bar the office of the president, dengo-tate industries, the

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:05.280
Lamy County government, and other respondents from a groundbreaking set for Wednesday, 30 September.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.320
The freeze stands until the court gives further directions.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.260
In the West Bank, about 100 Israeli settlers rioted and stopped an army operation meant

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.060
to take a Palestinian family home, Heret's reports.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.500
They burned structures and vehicles, threw stones, and wounded three Israeli officers.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.260
Three people were arrested.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.820
That family had faced continuous settler harassment, and a court had ordered the military to secure

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:30.380
their return.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.340
Also today, South Africa's Denel is upgrading Omani artillery under a contract worth

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:42.760
more than $2 billion Rand, about $122 million dollars, with a workshop in Oman and deliveries

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.420
phased through June 2030, Business Insider Africa reports.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.380
In Zimbabwe, two Cariba residents have asked the High Court to make the government put

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:56.980
adequate, safe, and reliable fairies on Lake Cariba, weeks after the Embuya-Nahonda disaster

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.640
killed 97 people.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.600
Nigeria's resident doctors have said a 14-day deadline for the government to meet welfare

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.980
and professional demands, or face a walkout, pointing to delays after earlier official commitments,

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:14.800
premium times reported. Yohane Wissa scored and made the second as the Democratic Republic of

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:22.060
the Congo beats Zimbabwe 2-1 in Harari, and Congo now leads Group E of the 2027 Africa Cup of

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.240
Nations Qualifiers, with six points, Al Jazeera reports. In the wider world, the food and agriculture

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.680
culture organization is asking for more money for farms and emergency food production in

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.620
Sudan, where the need still dwarfs the cash on hand.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.480
Rain Paulson, who leads the agency's emergencies in resilience office, said that to China daily

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.180
in Nairobi after a visit to Sudan last week.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.120
The work is aimed at staple crops, livestock health, and animal feed.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.140
A program that cost about $17 million last year produced more than $500 million of

00:03:54.140 --> 00:04:00.340
surgum, about 22% of Sudan's national crop. Vaccination is running nationwide, with feed

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:06.080
concentrates and minerals, and Paulson wants irrigation rebuilt so farmers are less tied to unreliable

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:11.740
rain. He calls the coming El Nino a food security risk multiplier for the horn. In Sudan,

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:17.860
rainfall may fall short by 30-40%, and it may come too late to plant. In Somalia,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.780
the fear is too much water, and floods in the Juba and Chebelle basins. The case on both sides

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:28.780
now is whether a sum sitting in a Serbian court account is enough after Belgrade sent

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.400
a Barani asylum seeker back to jail prison.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.200
Ahmed Jaffar Muhammad Ali has been there since January 2022.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.240
The Council of Europe's Committee of Ministers wants Serbia to carry out a European Court of

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.300
Human Rights Judgment from March 2025, Middle East I reports.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.200
That court found Serbia broke Article 3 of the European Convention, the ban on torture and

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:56.880
on inhuman or degrading treatment by extraditing him against an interim block and without examining

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.220
his fear of ill-treatment.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.600
The committee says Belgrade should work with Ali's representatives and the court's

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:08.880
secretaryate, so an award of 9,800 euros plus any tax and interest if payment defaults

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.360
can actually be released.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:16.600
Sayed Ahmed Awaday, of the Bahrain Institute for Rights and Democracy, says Serbia cannot

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:22.200
treat Bahrain's assurances as enough, and must do what it can to protect Ali. In an account,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:27.720
the paper says came from a recent call, Ali describes beatings, a packed cell in building two,

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.340
hunger strikes, and solitary confinement. His lawyers say the Interpol red notice that led to his

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:39.500
arrest in November 2021 was issued unlawfully. Campaigners say a private jet chartered by Royal

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.840
Jet based in the United Arab Emirates flew him to Bahrain three days after the interim measure.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:49.900
What the committee records on Serbia's side is that a sum for Ali now sits in a deposit

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.180
account in a domestic court, and that his lawyers say the conditions for releasing it

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.060
are hard to meet while he is in jail.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.260
He is held on two life sentences.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:03.620
He left Bahrain in 2011, lived in Iran, then went to Serbia to seek asylum.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.340
The shared record is the January 2022 extradition.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:13.780
Those two life sentences, the March 2025 finding, and the 9,800 euro award.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:18.420
The committee's next demand is cooperation so the money can be released without delay.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:24.980
A sign of progress, cholera cases in Sudan have fallen after humanitarian teams increase support

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.840
to contain the outbreak, africa.com reports.

